title: Switches and lights
check: on y
parts:
---- intro
Everything a computer does is made of **signals** that are either **0** (off) or **1** (on). That is all a wire in a digital circuit can carry.

On the right is the smallest circuit there is: a **switch** called `a`, wired to a **light** called `y`. The switch shows its value, 0 or 1. The wire between them carries that value to the light.
---- task
Click the switch `a` so the light `y` comes on.
---- start
input a 0 20
led y 220 20
a -> y
---- answer
input a 0 20
led y 220 20
a -> y
---- hint1
The switch is the box with a 0 in it, on the left of the circuit. Click it.
---- hint2
Click the 0 inside the box `a`: it becomes a 1, and the 1 travels along the wire to the light.
---- solution
Click the switch: its value becomes 1, the wire carries the 1, and the light turns on. Click it again and everything goes back to 0.
---- done
The light is on because the wire carries a **1**. Click the switch again and it turns off: the wire carries a **0**. In a circuit, nothing is ever "half on".
